  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1236 AM CDT Fri Sep 11 2026\n\nUnseasonably hot temperatures are forecast across West Central Texas \nthis weekend as an upper level ridge remains centered across \nOklahoma and North Texas. Highs on Saturday will be 10 to 15 degrees \nabove normal. Highs will be in the upper 90s to near 104. Highs on \nSunday will be a few degrees cooler than Saturday, but still well \nabove seasonal normals. Highs will be in the mid 90s to near 101. \n\nFor the early to middle part of next week, the upper level ridge \ndrifts east and becomes centered across the Southeast United States. \nThis ridge will extend well west into Texas continuing the above \nnormal temperatures and mainly dry conditions. Highs through this \nperiod will be in the mid 90s to near 100. Upper level lows will be \nin the upper 60s to mid 70s.",
